  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Providing-potable-water-to-thousands-in-india</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The lack of uncontaminated water for drinking, cooking and bathing is a serious problem in Odisha, one of India&apos;s most impoverished states. SevaChild International has installed clean water systems in two of Odisha&apos;s leper colonies, and has earmarked nine rural villages in Odisha that are without uncontaminated water. Villagers in some instances need to walk as far as five miles to find clean water that they take back to their homes via heavy pots -- a difficult task.</narrative>
  </description>
